// Test the stringify() depth guard (MaxDepthExceededError).
//
// The guard is best-effort, not an architectural guarantee: bootstrap is
// itself a Lox++ program run by the native VM, so stringify()'s own
// recursion shares the VM's call-frame budget (VM::FRAMES_MAX) with
// whatever call depth the caller already has. At a shallow call site (as
// here, top-level) the guard reliably fires well before that budget is
// exhausted; deep inside an already-deep call chain it can lose the race
// to a native "Stack overflow." instead. See notes/bootstrap-stack-depth.md.
// CHECK: caught: MaxDepthExceededError
// CHECK: after

var v = [];
var i = 0;
while (i < 150) {
    v = [v];
    i = i + 1;
}
try {
    print v;
} catch (e) {
    print "caught: " + e.kind;
}
print "after";
